Package: opstress
Title: Assign Operative Severity Scores to Current Procedural Terminology Codes
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Saieesh", "Rao", email = "saieesh.rao@northwestern.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6376-6172"))
Description: This package provides a data.frame containing operative severity
  scores, a validated measure of physiologic burden associated with different
  surgical cases. This score has been used in studies of frailty and its 
  association with mortality (see Shinall et. al, JAMA Surgery (2020)).
  A convenience function, `oss`, is included for mapping operative severity scores
  to CPT codes contained in data.frame variables or similar data structures. While
  this function is efficient for most applications, it includes an option for
  parallel processing which may be useful in larger data sets.
